course: dictionary
lesson: 5846
title: Malayalam: a language and an alphabet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Malayalam is a word with two meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. The first meaning is a language: «"Ammamma" is grandma in Malayalam.» Here Malayalam is the name of a language, because grandma is a word in it.
explain: The second meaning is an alphabet, the set of letters used to write a language. «The Malayalam letters are round and curly.» The words letters and round show that this sentence is about writing, not speaking.
explain: Malayalam is spoken by about 35 million people, mainly in the state of Kerala in south-west India. Many families from Kerala live in other countries, so a classmate may speak Malayalam at home.
fact: Malayalam is a language spoken by about 35 million people.
fact: Most Malayalam speakers live in the state of Kerala, in south-west India.
fact: Malayalam is one of the 22 official languages of India.
fact: Malayalam belongs to the Dravidian family of languages, like Tamil.
fact: The name Malayalam is a palindrome in English letters: it reads the same forwards and backwards.
exercise: «"Ammamma" is grandma in Malayalam.» What is Malayalam here? | A town in Australia | A type of boat | *A language, spoken mainly in Kerala in south-west India | A kind of fruit from Kerala
exercise: Which word reads the same forwards and backwards? | India | *Malayalam | Tamil | Kerala
exercise: About how many people speak Malayalam? | About 3 million | About 35 thousand | *About 35 million | About 350 million
test: «The Malayalam letters are round and curly.» What does Malayalam mean in this sentence? | A holiday in India | A grandma | *The alphabet used to write the language | A language spoken in Ireland
test: Malayalam is part of the same family as which other language? | Japanese | Scots | Spanish | *Tamil
exam: A friend says «"Ammamma" means grandma in my language.» Which language is she speaking? | *Malayalam | Australian English | Scots | Spanish
